  "changes_qualified": [
    "Windows project settings select Safe thread mode before the engine starts. No native binaries changed.",
    "Windows recovery writes both the plain and Windows-specific Compatibility keys; the shipped CMD launcher forces OpenGL and Safe before scripts and persists basic graphics without automatic calibration.",
    "Recovery cancel leaves settings untouched; acceptance restarts once, changes only graphics/renderer keys, and keeps the fallback file.",
    "An unpresented trial cannot be confirmed by waiting, pausing or closing. The actual completed menu makes the trial eligible. Failed menu trials retain Compatibility for the following launch.",
    "Windows renderer choice has two localized choices, platform-specific help and no Android experimental prompt. All new recovery strings and choices have EN/RU/DE coverage; controls and help are rendered and inspected at 800x600.",
    "Separate process launches verify launcher startup, persisted Compatibility without CLI renderer overrides, pending Forward+, and fallback after an unconfirmed run. The QA copy maps only the Windows override selector to Linux; scripts and persisted Windows policy are unchanged.",
    "Packaged Safe-thread Linux runtime completes the main-menu loading sequence, opens a Russian campaign, warms shaders and returns to the menu in both Forward+ and Compatibility.",
    "Existing Android renderer recovery and first-person action behavior pass regression checks. Browser update preserves every IndexedDB store, including save and data sentinels."
  ],
  "diagnostic_assessment": [
    "The supplied 1.11.0 report has all optional effects disabled while the engine is still Forward+ / D3D12 with Separate rendering. The final trace precedes presentation of the constructed 3D menu; the report screen itself works.",
    "The report does not contain a GPU reset code, thread backtrace or shader failure proving the exact hang. Safe threading and OpenGL recovery avoid the reported startup configuration; no claim is made that a driver defect was reproduced or repaired.",
    "Upstream Iris Xe D3D12 reports describe similar hardware but different explicit pipeline errors; they are supporting context, not a confirmed match."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/tutorials/editor/command_line_tutorial.html",
